# The turns of the inner loop are counted in front of it, so its fast copies do not poll on a turn: they poll between stretches of many turns, on a rare path.
# A turn of the outer loop runs a whole loop, so it polls once a row: the first poll of the function.
# The polls of the inner loop belong to the copy that keeps its checks and to the ways between two stretches.
# An unlikely path of the outer loop comes back in front of it. That way round has no other poll, so it polls on the way back: the last poll. What enters the outer loop from outside polls nowhere.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="total" role=Source
# CHECK: Patchpoint({{*}}isLoopPoll, {{*}}, [[outer]]:LoopHint)
# CHECK: Patchpoint({{*}}isLoopPoll, {{*}}:LoopHint)
# CHECK: Patchpoint({{*}}isLoopPoll, {{*}}, [[outer]]:LoopHint)
